# Lines tools/check-serial must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# Spike S2, on the Pi 5 only (systems/rpi5b_2gb/fb-test.system): the
# display test pattern QEMU's display-test draws, at 2x, centred, in the
# firmware's 1920x1080 framebuffer, read back. The pattern's hash is of its
# 800x480 Xrgb8888 rows, as QEMU's ramfb holds them; the second, of every
# x8r8g8b8 byte written. crates/nowayos-display/tests/test_pattern.rs computes
# both from nowayos_display::test_pattern, so the chain is closed.
NOWAYOS: fb-test: starting
NOWAYOS: fb-test: the board's framebuffer: 1920x1080 x8r8g8b8, 7680 bytes a row, its window from row 0
NOWAYOS: fb-test: the 800x480 test pattern, hash 0x26a5f77654fa9525, shown at 2x at (160, 60)
NOWAYOS: fb-test: wrote 1600x960 x8r8g8b8 pixels, hash 0x52965e6e8dfa7f25; read back the same

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# the PD giving up, or a read-back that differs.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!which differs
